module examples.err_layout_offset_overflow

# plans/M7.md item I (the adversarial sweep), 03-hardware.md §3: "For
# every `@layout` type the compiler reports exact size, offsets, padding,
# and endianness".
#
# `@offset(n)` decodes any `n` a `u64` holds, and `check_one_layout` then
# did `offset + size` twice — once to decide whether a mis-ordered field
# *overlaps* its predecessor, and once to advance the layout cursor.
# Neither addition was checked.
#
# WHAT THAT WAS. In a debug build, `wrela dump --stage=layout-types` on
# this file panicked ("attempt to add with overflow") out of
# `sema/types.rs` — a crash, not a diagnostic. In a release build the
# addition would have *wrapped*: `cursor` would become 0, so this layout
# would report `size=0`. A zero-byte `@layout(dma)` type is a DMA pool of
# `count` slots and zero bytes of backing (`img.dma_pool`'s own
# `count × sizeof(T)`), and every subsequent field would be accepted at
# offset 0 on top of every other — the exact fail-open 03 §2/§3 exist to
# prevent, produced by a declaration a user can write.
#
# It is rejected before either addition runs now, by the fact that is
# actually wrong: the field's last byte does not exist.
#
# Sibling rejections, each its own golden: `err-layout-offset-outside`
# (an `@offset` inside a *non*-`@layout` struct), `err-layout-overlap`
# (two fields sharing bytes), `err-layout-order` (descending offsets),
# `err-layout-unaligned-offset` (an `@offset` its own width does not
# divide).

@layout(dma, endian=little)
struct Huge:
    a: u8
    @offset(0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) z: u8
